---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import LearningProgress from '../../components/LearningProgress.astro';
import { lessons, learningStages } from '../../lib/learning';
import { url } from '../../lib/url';
import '../../styles/learning.css';
---
<Base title="Learn step by step · Gradient Ascent" description="An 18-lesson path from model basics to operating agents, with worked examples, exercises, explained answers, and six projects.">
  <div class="page-hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">Start here · No coding required to begin</div>
    <h1>Learn step by step</h1>
    <p>Build understanding before adding autonomy. Follow 18 lessons through six stages, with a worked example and a self-check in each lesson.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="learn-intro">
    <p>Start at the beginning or revisit a stage. The sequence is a teaching order; the site's eight levels describe how much control a model has. Higher levels are not a score or a destination everyone needs to reach.</p>
    <p>Allow roughly 4–5 hours for the lessons, plus time for the projects and optional reading. These are planning estimates. In every lesson, start with a prefilled English message, press Send, and watch a sample reply appear. Review it, then send the suggested follow-up. No JSON editing, installation, API key, or paid model is needed.</p>
    <p>These are guided conversations with scripted replies, not live model calls. Editing a message does not change the reply yet. Optional configuration exercises show how an application enforces its rules. All six projects can be written here in your own words. Drafts and progress stay in this browser, with downloads for your own copy. Mark completion yourself when you can explain the result.</p>
  </div>
  <LearningProgress />
  <nav aria-label="Learning stages" class="stage-jumps">
    {learningStages.map((stage, i) => <a href={`#stage-${i + 1}`}>{i + 1}. {stage.title}</a>)}
  </nav>
  {learningStages.map((stage, i) => <section class="learn-stage" id={`stage-${i + 1}`}>
    <div class="eyebrow">Stage {i + 1} of 6</div>
    <h2>{stage.title}</h2><p>{stage.summary}</p>
    <ol class="lesson-list" start={i * 3 + 1}>
      {lessons.filter(l => l.stage === i).map(l => <li>
        <div><a href={url(`/learn/${l.id}/`)}>{l.title}</a><p>{l.objective}</p></div>
        <small>~{l.minutes} min <span data-lesson-badge={l.id}></span></small>
      </li>)}
    </ol>
    <div class="stage-project">
      <h3>Stage project: {stage.project}</h3>
      <ul>{stage.deliverables.map(d => <li>{d}</li>)}</ul>
      <p><strong>Ready to continue when:</strong> {stage.ready}</p>
      <p><a href={url(`/learn/${lessons.filter(l => l.stage === i).at(-1)!.id}/#stage-project`)}>Open this project workspace →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>)}
  <p class="learn-intro">The path introduces the major ideas; the linked concept pages add diagrams, examples, limitations, and primary sources. It is not a complete machine-learning degree or a qualification for safety-critical deployment.</p>
</Base>
